{
  "id": "u01-l04",
  "unit": "u01-basics",
  "title": "How are you?",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**আছ-** (*achh-*) means 'to be (in a state / somewhere)'. Its ending changes with the person:\n\n- আমি **আছি** (*achhi*): I am\n- তুমি **আছো** (*achho*): you (familiar) are\n- আপনি **আছেন** (*achhen*): you (polite) are\n\nPolite আপনি forms almost always end in **-েন**, so **কেমন আছেন?** is polite and **কেমন আছো?** is familiar. The pronoun is often dropped because the ending already says who you mean.\n\nUseful words: **ভালো** (*bhalo*) good, **খুব** (*khub*) very, **আর** (*ar*) and. In Bangladesh many people answer **আলহামদুলিল্লাহ, ভালো আছি** ('praise be to God, I'm well').\n\nSneak peek at the alphabet: the letter quiz is ভ as in ভালো.",
  "vocab": [
    {
      "id": "kemon",
      "bn": "কেমন",
      "tr": "kemon",
      "en": "how"
    },
    {
